{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"California security deposit cap (AB 12)","requirement":"A landlord may not charge a security deposit above one month's rent; owners of only two rental properties with four or fewer total units may charge up to two months' rent.","key_value":"1 month's rent; up to 2 months' rent for small landlords, from July 1, 2024","coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies statewide; the two-month amount applies to landlords owning only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC of natural persons.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":true,"other":"two-month cap only for owners of two or fewer rental properties with four or fewer residential units total"},"exemptions":"Landlords who own only two rental properties with no more than four residential units total, held by a natural person, family trust, or LLC whose members are natural persons, may charge up to two months' rent.","penalty":null,"effective_date":"2024-07-01","citation":"AB 12","quoted_span":"Starting July 1, 2024, many landlords may only charge one month's rent for unfurnished and furnished units","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Deadline to return security deposit with itemized deductions","requirement":"A landlord must return the deposit or remaining portion within 21 days after the tenant vacates, with a written itemized statement of deductions, and may deduct only amounts reasonably necessary for rent default, damage beyond wear and tear, and cleaning.","key_value":"21 days","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies; last month's rent counts as part of the deposit, first month's rent does not.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Board, Security Deposits","quoted_span":"All or any remaining portion of a security deposit must be returned within 21 days after the tenant/s leave the unit vacant.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Photograph unit at start of new tenancy","requirement":"A landlord must photograph the unit immediately before or at the start of a new tenancy to document its condition.","key_value":"photograph at start of tenancy, from July 1, 2025","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies that begin on or after July 1, 2025.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"tenancies beginning on or after 2025-07-01"},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-07-01","citation":"Berkeley Rent Board, Security Deposits","quoted_span":"For tenancies that begin on or after July 1, 2025, a landlord must photograph the unit immediately before or at the start of a new tenancy to document the condition of the unit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Post-possession photos and proof of repairs for deposit deductions","requirement":"Landlords must photograph the unit after regaining possession but before any repair or cleaning they will deduct for, and give the photos and a written cost explanation to the tenant; from January 1, 2025 they must prove necessary repairs were completed.","key_value":"photos before repairs, from April 1, 2025","coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies where the landlord makes a security deposit deduction for repairs or cleaning.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":"2025-04-01","citation":"Berkeley Rent Board, Security Deposits","quoted_span":"Starting April 1, 2025, landlords must take photographs of a unit after regaining possession, but before any repairs or cleaning for which the landlord intends to make a deduction from the security deposit.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Pre-move-out walk-through inspection offer","requirement":"A landlord must offer the tenant a walk-through inspection during the last two weeks of the tenancy so the tenant can correct items that would otherwise be deducted from the deposit.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All residential tenancies.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":null},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Board, Security Deposits","quoted_span":"Under state law, landlords must offer a walk-through inspection during the last two weeks of a tenancy to identify any items that need repair/cleaning.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D007-01","doc_id":"D007","jurisdiction":"Berkeley, CA","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance security deposit interest","requirement":"Landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year, plus a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","key_value":"annual interest on deposit","coverage_conditions":"Tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance.","applicability":{"built_on_or_before":null,"built_after":null,"date_basis":null,"min_units":null,"max_units":null,"owner_dependent":false,"other":"units fully or partially covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance"},"exemptions":"Units not covered by the Berkeley Rent Ordinance.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"citation":"Berkeley Rent Ordinance","quoted_span":"For tenancies in units fully or partially covered by Berkeley's Rent Ordinance, landlords must pay tenants interest on their security deposit at the end of each year and a prorated amount if the tenant moves out before the end of the year.","interaction":null,"confidence":0.8,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
